From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:59:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: NAK_UNROLL_DYN, unroll loops with a run-time trip count

Innermost loops of the shape "body; if (i + off == n) break" (or >=,
signed or unsigned), with i a counter stepping by 1 and n defined before
the loop, run N iterations per pass when a guard shows that none of the
first N - 1 ends the loop, one otherwise.  Every iteration runs as before
and in the same order; the N copies are one block, which the schedulers
can interleave, and the loop branch is taken once per N iterations.  The
reference compiler unrolls 88825d04's lighting loop 8 times.

Bodies are limited to ALU instructions and reorderable loads.  A shader the
pass changed is also compiled without it, and the unrolled variant is kept
unless it has fewer warps per SM.  Off by default (0); 2-8 copies.
---
